e1c2918acc58a74c368c3dd34a557466e84f04ea07e860cf","order":1,"original_content_hash":"sha256:e40515d97cb97120e1c2918acc58a74c368c3dd34a557466e84f04ea07e860cf","parser":{"profile_hash":"sha256:578fb774d074186da025b3047bd12691225b3688122f45aa8993f633e49a826a"},"physical_order":1,"raw_blob_id":"d005d467-6d0a-57d6-a23b-16dae3063f18","raw_file_hash":"sha256:1d018b71860e09de6c6878a2c5dc43ee180c15f68797bce2a72f1188657d5f2c","source_chapter_id":"body","source_locator":{"container_path":null,"field":"text","offset_kind":"HTML_SELECTOR","original_byte_offset":null,"path":"hydraulics-16.html","record":1,"selector":".mt-content-container"},"text":"A\nflow control valve\nis a specialized hydraulic valve designed to\nregulate the speed of actuators\nby controlling fluid flow. It combines two key components in a single body:\nA\nneedle valve\n, which will be used to\nrestrict flow in one direction\n, controlling the actuator speed\nA\ncheck valve\n, which\nallows free flow in the opposite direction\n, preventing unnecessary restriction when the flow direction changes\nThis design is especially useful in\nbi-directional actuator circuits\n, where different speeds are required for the forward and return strokes. For instance, a hydraulic cylinder may need to extend\nslowly\nwhile retracting\nquickly\n. By installing a flow control valve in the return line, fluid flow can be unrestricted in one direction, ensuring a\nrapid retraction\n, while controlled restriction in the opposite direction ensures a\nsteady and controlled extension speed\n.","title":"15.1: The Function of a Flow Control Valve","volume":"","work_id":"hydraulics-16","work_title":"hydraulics-16"}],"work_id":"hydraulics-16"}